receiveCctpV2Message.t.sol
├── given the message length is invalid, or its recipient is not the CCTP TokenMessenger, or its mint recipient is not this adapter
│  └── it should revert with InvalidCctpMessage
└── given the message is well-formed and addressed to the CCTP TokenMessenger and this adapter
   ├── given the CCTP MessageTransmitter fails to receive the message
   │  └── it should revert with CctpMessageReceptionFailed
   └── given the CCTP MessageTransmitter successfully receives the message
      ├── given the hash of the received message was not registered beforehand
      │  └── it should revert with UnexpectedMessage
      └── given the hash of the received message was registered beforehand
         ├── given the message contains an invalid recipient chain ID
         │  └── it should revert with InvalidRecipientChainId
         └── given the message contains a valid recipient chain ID
            ├── given the message contains an invalid output token address
            │  └── it should revert with InvalidOutputToken
            └── given the message contains a valid output token address
               ├── given the adapter received some amount of output token smaller than expected
               │  └── it should revert with MaxValueLossExceeded
               └── given the adapter received an amount of output token not smaller than expected
                  ├── given the input amount specified in the message is smaller than received amount
                  │  └── it should revert with InvalidInputAmount
                  └── given the input amount specified in the message is not smaller than received amount
                     ├── it should emit an InBridgeTransferReceived event
                     ├── it should increase the nextInTransferId in the receiving adapter
                     └── it should hold the received amount net of the CCTP fee, the fee having been paid to the fee receiver
